  "body": "### What is the issue with the Compatibility Standard?\n\nhttps://compat.spec.whatwg.org/#ua-string-section seems to mostly describe the status quo, per its description:\r\n\r\n> This section serves as a descriptive record of the User-Agent patterns found in the so-called major web browsers\r\n\r\nIt would probably be good to explicitly mark this as informative? (e.g., via Bikeshed's [informative classes](https://speced.github.io/bikeshed/#metadata-informative-classes))\r\n\r\nI mean the alternative is to make this fully normative, and require implementations to use specific user agent strings (presumably tied to the [navigator compatibility mode](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/system-state.html#concept-navigator-compatibility-mode)), but that seems like it would be a much more substantive change than what I believe the current intention is?",
